@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:privacy;security] susan-content-free-relay
Susan relays only an opaque end-to-end ciphertext, a collapse id and a closed
notification kind. It MUST NOT receive, derive or store message content,
terminal bytes, routes or Marshall identifiers beyond the delivery id used for
dedupe. Provider payloads carry only the ciphertext, collapse id and
localization keys chosen from the kind.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:privacy] susan-no-addresses-or-tokens-at-rest
Provider tokens exist only inside AEAD-sealed push keys held by Marshall.
Susan MUST NOT persist or log provider tokens, push-key envelopes, ciphertext,
install public keys or source addresses. Source addresses are reduced in memory
to an HMAC under a daily random salt; the negative cache stores only a keyed
token digest.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] susan-audit-append-only
Audit entries are append-only in PostgreSQL (trigger plus REVOKE), hash
chained through prev_digest and pruned only by the audited 90-day retention
job. Operators read, verify and export the trail only through bin/susan rpc;
there is no network admin surface.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] susan-fixed-provider-egress
Outbound HTTP MUST go only to the fixed APNs, Google OAuth and FCM origins with
verify_peer TLS against the system trust store. Configuration cannot add an
origin; service accounts naming any other token endpoint are refused.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] susan-runtime-secret-custody
Secrets arrive only as files in $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY (systemd credentials
from the overallsSecrets bundle, or a container secrets mount). Every file
passes the canonical-path, ancestor, single-link, ownership and mode checks;
any failure is the single fixed startup error without contents or paths.
